@startuml data-timing
title Radar V1 batch data shapes, implementation stage, and execution questions
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

legend right
Green: bounded implementation evidence.
Yellow: confirmed responsibility/contract; full path incomplete.
Red: method, ordering, or execution remains open.
endlegend

package "Illustrative batch data organization; DDC behavior evidenced separately" {
  component "DDC data\n[N,64] complex\n12.5 MS/s/channel candidate" as D #B7E1CD
  component "Commanded azimuth beamformed\n[N,4] complex elevation streams" as B #B7E1CD
  component "Range processing\n[rangeBin,pulse,elevation]" as R #FFF2CC
  component "Pulse accumulation + range-migration\nhandling; prepare slow-time ensemble\ninitially without compensation" as ACC #FFF2CC
  component "Doppler data\n[rangeBin,dopplerBin,elevation]" as V #FFF2CC
  D --> B
  B --> R
  R --> ACC
  ACC --> V
}

package "Future Simulink representations: fixed dimensions per configured model" {
  component "Behavioral model first\napproved algorithms / interfaces;\nnot required to be cycle-accurate" as BEHAV #FFF2CC
  component "Later hardware-oriented\nimplementation model" as HW #FFF2CC
  component "HDL generation\ndeferred" as HDL #F4CCCC
  BEHAV --> HW : may follow
  HW ..> HDL : future; no readiness implied
}

component "Rates, sample/frame execution,\nbuffer owner, corner-turn implementation,\nlatency, and execution granularity" as OPEN #F4CCCC
V .. OPEN : unresolved Simulink boundary details

note bottom of D
DDC bounded evidence: 372 ADC-tick group delay (31 output samples);
state retained across PRI/transition boundaries. MATLAB accepts variable
frame lengths while preserving continuous state; Simulink dimensions are fixed
per configured model and do not allow runtime-variable frame sizes.
end note

note bottom of R
These tensors show batch data organization only, not settled streaming module
interfaces. The pulse axis represents per-pulse range results; the separate
accumulation responsibility prepares the slow-time ensemble.
end note

note bottom of V
Accepted timing evidence: five PRFs; usable pulse counts [22,25,28,32,35];
151 schedule records; 10,553,388 ADC ticks under the 10,597,950-tick cap.
This schedule evidence does not demonstrate end-to-end detection performance.
end note
@enduml
